SplashOutputDev builds a lookup table with 1 << BitsPerComponent entries for
one-component images, and GfxImageColorMap accepts up to 30 bits.
drawImage() allocates it with gmallocn_checkoverflow() and renders without
the table when that fails; drawMaskedImage() used gmallocn(), which aborts
("Bogus memory allocation size") once n * 3 or n * 4 overflows int. Use the
checked allocation there too. drawSoftMaskedImage() allocated the soft mask's
table (1 GB for 30 bits, abort when that fails) although ImageStream pixels
are bytes and the table is never indexed past 255: cap it at 256 entries.

Not fixed upstream as of d828315.
Upstream: none found (poppler/poppler issues and MRs searched for
drawMaskedImage, "lookup table", "Bogus memory allocation size").

